@{
    Layout = "_Layout";
    ViewData["Title"] = "The World Cup Tournament Kicks Off in Mexico City";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Sixteen years ago, a thunderous left-footed strike from Siphiwe Tshabalala and a sea of buzzing vuvuzelas in Johannesburg ushered in a new era of football.";
}

@section Styles {
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/newsdetail.css" />
}

<article class="container nd-article">
    <!-- Article Header -->
    <div class="article-header">
        <div class="article-meta">
            <span class="badge-live">Tournament News</span>
            <span>Published: May 27, 2026</span>
            <span>By Editorial Team</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="article-title">The World Cup Tournament Kicks Off in Mexico City</h1>
        <p class="article-subheading">In a poetic twist of fate, co-hosts Mexico will kick off the biggest-ever FIFA World Cup against South Africa, reversing the roles of their iconic 2010 opening-match stalemate.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Article Hero Image -->
    <img src="/media/mex-rsa.jpeg" alt="The World Cup Tournament Kicks Off in Mexico City" class="article-hero-image" />

    <!-- Article Content Grid -->
    <div class="article-body-wrapper">
        <!-- Main Body Text -->
        <div class="article-body">
            <p>Sixteen years ago, a thunderous left-footed strike from Siphiwe Tshabalala and a sea of buzzing vuvuzelas in Johannesburg ushered in a new era of football. On June 11, 2026, history comes full circle. In a poetic twist of fate, co-hosts Mexico will kick off the biggest-ever FIFA World Cup against South Africa, reversing the roles of their iconic 2010 opening-match stalemate.</p>

            <h3 class="nd-heading">A Rematch for the Ages</h3>
            <p>The 2010 World Cup opener between South Africa and Mexico remains one of the most memorable matches in recent history. The 1-1 draw at Soccer City set the tone for a thrilling tournament. Now, the stage is set at the iconic Estadio Azteca in Mexico City, where over 80,000 passionate fans are expected to witness another historic clash.</p>

            <blockquote class="nd-blockquote">
                "It's a beautiful coincidence. The memories of 2010 are still fresh in our minds, and to face South Africa again in an opening match, this time on our home turf, is incredibly special." - Mexican National Team Coach
            </blockquote>

            <p>South Africa, affectionately known as Bafana Bafana, comes into the tournament with a blend of experienced veterans and exciting young talent. Their recent performances in the Africa Cup of Nations have shown they are a team not to be underestimated.</p>

            <p>Mexico, meanwhile, carries the weight of a nation's expectations. Playing at the Estadio Azteca offers a formidable home advantage, but the pressure to deliver a victory in the opening match will be immense. The tactical battle between the two teams promises to be as intriguing as their historical narrative.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Sidebar -->
        <aside class="article-sidebar">
            <h3 class="sidebar-title">Tournament Facts</h3>
            <div class="nd-facts-container">
                <div class="nd-fact-item-bordered">
                    <span>Start Date:</span>
                    <span class="nd-fact-value">June 11, 2026</span>
                </div>
                <div class="nd-fact-item-bordered">
                    <span>End Date:</span>
                    <span class="nd-fact-value">July 19, 2026</span>
                </div>
                <div class="nd-fact-item-bordered">
                    <span>Teams:</span>
                    <span class="nd-fact-value">48 (Expanded)</span>
                </div>
                <div class="nd-fact-item">
                    <span>Matches:</span>
                    <span class="nd-fact-value">104 Matches</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </aside>
    </div>
</article>
